## 🟢 Priority 3 — Data Integrity (Sharpness Logic Audit)

The Laplacian Variance auto-snap logic in [auto_capture.py](file:///c:/Users/ericd/Documents/MyVertexProject/AJ%27s%20AI%20Coin%20Collection%20app/auto_capture.py) is **sound**. Here's the verified gate chain:

```
Frame read → Laplacian.var() → sharpness_score
                                      ↓
                     > MIN_SHARPNESS_FLOOR (2000)?  → No → bar stays Red, no snap
                                      ↓ Yes
                     > (max_sharpness * 0.8)?        → No → bar stays Yellow
                                      ↓ Yes
                     is_stable (15 stable frames)?   → No → wait
                                      ↓ Yes
                     Last snap > 4s ago?             → No → cooldown
                                      ↓ Yes
                              ✅ cv2.imwrite() fires
```

> [!TIP]
> The `MIN_SHARPNESS_FLOOR = 2000.0` was calibrated for LED lighting. If the Jiusion microscope light is at low power, raise it to `1500`. If captures are blurry, raise it to `2500`.

One minor concern: `max_sharpness` decays aggressively on line 113:
```python
if sharpness_score < (max_sharpness * 0.5):
    max_sharpness = sharpness_score  # ← Resets the "peak" reference suddenly
```
This can cause the "SUCCESS ZONE" marker to jump. A smoother approach is an exponential moving average:
```python
max_sharpness = max_sharpness * 0.95 + sharpness_score * 0.05  # gentle decay
```

